{"diagnosis": "Loopback sends 0xa5 but trace ends with `TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received` and `FAIL 0xdead`, so recv_buf_valid never asserts. Expected state 0 to advance 0->1 on start-bit (!ser_rx) to sample the byte, but excerpt line 80 holds `recv_state <= 0` in state 0 so the receiver stays in idle forever. This stuck-idle transition alone explains the 22023-cycle timeout; CONE_SLICE has no simpleuart driver refs so trace plus excerpt decide.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 			case (recv_state)
 				0: begin
 					if (!ser_rx)
-						recv_state <= 0;
+						recv_state <= 1;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (byte 0xa5 received), no `TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received`"}

